A_PROGRAM_DIMENSION_ACTION 1

status EXPERIMENTAL_KERNEL_CONTRACT
direction BINARY_ENDPOINTS
face_digit ENDPOINT_0=0 ENDPOINT_1=1 VARYING=2
action_result EXECUTABLE=1 RESIDUAL=2 UNSUPPORTED=3 INVALID=4

The dimension action is an object-language operation on the common Core Term
graph.  It is not a generated TypeDeclaration, a solver request identity, a
conversion rule, or a value/computation polarity tag.

An n-dimensional face key is a vector of n face digits.  Its intrinsic
dimension is the number of VARYING digits.  The all-VARYING key is the center.
Every other key is a boundary face.  Dimension zero has one center and no
boundary.

For deterministic APP-spine construction, boundary keys are traversed in
lexicographic base-three order with the leftmost axis most significant and the
center omitted.  This order is owned by the dimension module.  Callers must
not reproduce its cardinality or ordering.  The boundary count is 3^n - 1 and
must be computed with checked arithmetic.

A dimension operator from source dimension n to target dimension m is an
immutable vector of n source-axis images.  Each image is ENDPOINT_0,
ENDPOINT_1, or one target axis in [0,m).  Target axes not named by an image are
new varying directions.  The first implementation is affine: a target axis
may occur in at most one source-axis image.  Duplicate target axes, an
out-of-range target axis, malformed storage, or an arithmetic overflow makes
the operator INVALID.

The identity operator id_n maps source axis i to target axis i.  The canonical
extension operator e_n : n -> n+1 maps source axis i to target axis i and
leaves target axis n new.  The initial object identity action uses e_0.
Repeated higher identity uses e_1, e_2, and so on; no dimension-specific Term
tag or declaration is introduced.

An operator acts contravariantly on a target face key by replacing every
source-axis image with its endpoint constant or the digit at its referenced
target axis.  Composition f : n -> m followed by g : m -> k substitutes every
axis image of f through g and produces g o f : n -> k.  Composition is INVALID
when dimensions do not meet or when the affine target-axis condition would be
violated.  Identity is a two-sided unit.  Composition is associative for all
valid operators.  Interning compares the complete semantic vector, not an
allocation or request ID.

The Core form is:

  DIMENSION_ACTION(source_term, operator_id)

The operator source dimension must equal the dimension certified for the
source Term.  The result dimension is the operator target dimension.  An
ordinary source Term has certified dimension zero.  An uninstantiated nested
DIMENSION_ACTION has the target dimension of its outer operator.  Boundary APP
instantiation does not create another dimension operator.

For an acted family of target dimension n, the classifier exposes every
required boundary face in the canonical traversal order as an ordinary
dependent Pi telescope.  Applying those arguments uses ordinary APP Terms and
APP_ELIM.  The final result is the center family or center witness.  A missing
boundary is an ordinary partial application.  An extra boundary, a boundary
with the wrong classifier, or a noncanonical forged classifier is rejected by
ordinary dependent APP checking and action-certificate replay.

TypeDeclarationDB remains authority only for source-defined and imported
ADT/IADT schemas.  Acting on an ADT recursively reads the source declaration,
source constructor ordinal, source field telescope, operator, and already
acted Context prefix.  It must not allocate a TypeDeclaration or assign a new
constructor ordinal.  An acted constructor retains the source declaration and
source constructor identity through its source Term child.

Classifier dispatch for version 1 is:

  source ADT/IADT type       EXECUTABLE through a read-only acted schema view
  source constructor        EXECUTABLE by incremental telescope action
  nondependent pure Pi      EXECUTABLE pointwise
  dependent Pi              RESIDUAL until dependent family lifting is replayed
  pure Return               EXECUTABLE when its value action is executable
  pure Thunk                EXECUTABLE when its computation action is executable
  Lambda                    EXECUTABLE from accepted Lambda/body derivations
  APP                       EXECUTABLE from accepted function/argument derivations
  Match                     EXECUTABLE for the admitted derivation-driven fragment
  induction hypothesis      EXECUTABLE for the admitted guarded-IH fragment
  empty-effect computation  EXECUTABLE only through the listed pure forms
  effectful computation     RESIDUAL
  unresolved effect row     RESIDUAL
  operation request         RESIDUAL
  computation fold          RESIDUAL
  resource-sensitive term  RESIDUAL until a modality/usage action is represented
  Universe                  UNSUPPORTED in version 1
  host primitive            UNSUPPORTED in version 1
  malformed source proof    INVALID
  malformed operator        INVALID

An implementation may strengthen a RESIDUAL case only after this schema and
its replay rule are revised.  It must not silently reinterpret RESIDUAL as
UNSUPPORTED or as proof of an empty identity family.

The new Judgement proof kinds are:

  DIMENSION_ACTION_TYPE_FORMATION=45
  DIMENSION_ACTION_TERM=46
  DIMENSION_ACTION_CONSTRUCTOR=47

DIMENSION_ACTION_TYPE_FORMATION concludes that an acted type is a type.  Its
ordered premises are:

  0 source IS_TYPE Claim
  1 exact acted classifier IS_TYPE Claim when the classifier is not Universe
  2..n exact Context/substitution/type-formation Claims required by the
       source-former-specific replay rule

DIMENSION_ACTION_TERM concludes that the action of a typed ordinary Term has
the exact acted classifier.  Its ordered premises are:

  0 source HAS_TYPE Claim
  1 source classifier IS_TYPE Claim
  2 acted classifier IS_TYPE Claim
  3..n exact syntax-directed Claims for Lambda, APP, Match, IH, Return, or
       Thunk action, in source-child order

DIMENSION_ACTION_CONSTRUCTOR is distinct because its theorem quantifies over a
source declaration and an incrementally acted field telescope.  Its ordered
premises are:

  0 source constructor HAS_TYPE Claim
  1 source owner type-formation Claim
  2 acted owner type-formation Claim
  3..n acted field classifier and field witness Claims in source-field order

The conclusion Term for all three rules contains only the source Term and the
semantic operator ID.  Context-action requests, work IDs, caches, and fuel do
not occur in Term identity.  APP_ELIM remains the sole proof rule for applying
explicit boundary Terms after the acted family has been formed.

Action preserves an empty effect row.  It does not erase, execute, commute, or
handle an effect.  A nonempty or unresolved effect row is RESIDUAL.  Likewise,
version 1 does not duplicate, discard, or reorder a resource-sensitive
binding; such a Context action is RESIDUAL.

Normalization may remove DIMENSION_ACTION(t,id_n) only after the source Term
has certified dimension n.  It may replace nested actions

  DIMENSION_ACTION(DIMENSION_ACTION(t,f),g)

with DIMENSION_ACTION(t,g o f) only when composition is valid and no explicit
boundary APP has intervened.  No other action equation is DefEq in version 1.

In particular, an inhabited object identity produced by dimension action does
not add a conversion equation, merge Term IDs, mutate a global equality
union-find, or authorize equality reflection.  Object identity remains an
ordinary type with ordinary proof Terms, Claims, and Derivations.

Dimension one, two, and three therefore use the same constructions:

  A1 = DIMENSION_ACTION(A,e_0)                    boundary count 2
  A2 = DIMENSION_ACTION(A1,e_1)                   boundary count 8
  A3 = DIMENSION_ACTION(A2,e_2)                   boundary count 26

No rule identifies a square by index count eight, and no generated
TypeDeclaration identity appears in this specification.
